course: dictionary
lesson: 8140
title: Represent: standing for, speaking for, showing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word represent has several meanings, and context tells you which one to use. «A red cross represents first aid.» Here represent means stands for: the red cross is a sign that means first aid. Try it: "a red cross stands for first aid" still makes sense.
explain: «She represents our class on the council.» Now represent means speaks and acts for a group. Swap in "speaks for" and the sentence still works. The clue is that she is one person sitting for the whole class.
explain: «An MP represents everyone in their area, including children who cannot vote yet.» An MP is a Member of Parliament. The clue is "everyone in their area": represent means to speak and act for all the people who live there, not just the ones who can vote.
fact: Represent is a verb: I represent, she represents, they represented, we are representing.
fact: To represent can mean to stand for something, as a symbol does: «a red cross represents first aid».
fact: To represent can mean to speak or act for a person or group: «an MP represents their area».
fact: To represent can mean to show something in a drawing, model or chart: «bar charts represent data».
fact: A «constituent» is a person who lives in the area an MP represents.
exercise: «A red cross represents first aid.» What does represents mean here? | Runs very fast | *Stands for, is a sign of | Cuts or wounds | Is painted in the colour blue
exercise: «She represents our class on the council.» What does represents mean here? | *Speaks and acts for our class | Sleeps in the classroom | Draws a picture of our class | Is taller than the whole class
exercise: In maths, «x represents the unknown.» What does represents mean? | *Stands for | Forgets | Counts backwards | Hides
test: Who does an MP represent? | Only the people who can vote | *Everyone who lives in their area | Nobody at all | Only their own family
test: «A US president does not represent any local area.» What does this tell you? | A US president is only for children | *A US president is not the local voice for one particular area | A US president draws maps | A US president lives in every town
exam: Which meaning of represent fits «This change represents a big step forward»? | Hides the forward step | *Is the same as, or amounts to | Speaks for a class | Draws a picture of a step
